Z||000000||EMF||04-27-99||10:07 PM||||my 84 2m4 has lean exhaust, diagnostic code 44, what should i do, i dont have any sure-idea on   what would cause this, <br>the  ECM stores the diagnostic codes from the last time the engine light came on right?<br>if i remember it  was in the middle of a  3 mile very steep hill and i had it floored
Z||000001||theogre||04-27-99||10:24 PM||||reset the ECM and watch for when/if it reapears.<p>A lean mix at WOT under high load is a problem you don't want to ignore. it can fry the motor. but you need to know just what sets it off.<p>For example a 44 caused by WOT for a long time, like a hill climb, could mean that the injector(s), fuel filter, or the Fuel pump, are not flowing enough. 
Z||000002||EMF||04-27-99||10:46 PM||||ok, can do, worst case, what could it be?<br>the guy i bought the car from was anything but nice to it, he dosnt have a license, which tells you a bit about his car habbits, he didnt put 200 miles on it before the drivers side control arm ripped out, i hope he didnt have a chance to fuck anything else up, ;\
Z||000003||EMF||04-27-99||10:48 PM||||oh yea, one more dumb question, there are 2 slots on my fuse box <br>tbi inj1 <br>tbi inj2<br>i think thats what they were 1 & 2<br>should there be fuse's in these, i imagine the the tbi inj wouldnt work without them<br>
Z||000004||theogre||04-28-99||03:36 PM||||the injX fuses are only used in v6 aplications.<p>Could be anything. Vac leak, EGR lose/flaky, any of the stuff above. It's all relativly small stuff except the fuel pump which is a really huge pain.<p>If the TBI unit has any problems just rebuild it, put in a new TPS sensor and injector when you do. (all gaskets and the fuel reg diaphram are in the rebuild kit. which for mine was about 45$. the 86 back use a diferant kit so I don't know the price.)
